  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the first experiment should establish a strong multimodal baseline to anchor the search. config_010 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) pairs the most expressive RNA encoder (scgpt, a pretrained transformer capturing gene-gene context) with a solid but cost-effective image encoder (resnet50) and a cheap aggregation (avgpool) plus weighted fusion. This tests whether the combination of a learned RNA encoder with moderate image features and simple aggregation yields competitive accuracy, giving a high-quality reference point. It avoids the highest-cost stack (ViT-L + transformer aggregation) while still using the strongest RNA encoder, so the expected relative cost is medium-high (~60-70% of the most expensive multimodal config). If this performs well, subsequent experiments can probe whether upgrading the image encoder to ViT-L or the aggregation to transformer yields meaningful gains; if it underperforms, I learn that the bottleneck lies elsewhere (e.g., fusion strategy or profile setting) and can redirect exploration efficiently within the remaining 9 experiments."
}

